WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
Settle somewhere safe and still, with the feet, seat, or back supported.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.910
This practice includes optional small movements.

3
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:14.180
Make them smaller, imagine them, or leave them out if movement is uncomfortable.

4
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.940
Nothing should be forced through pain.

5
00:00:26.212 --> 00:00:28.612
Begin by noticing the shoulders without changing them.

6
00:00:30.312 --> 00:00:34.022
Sense their height, weight, temperature, and contact with clothing.

7
00:00:35.722 --> 00:00:38.042
One may sit higher or feel clearer than the other.

8
00:00:39.742 --> 00:00:42.892
Let the difference be information rather than a problem.

9
00:00:57.781 --> 00:01:01.601
If it feels comfortable, lift both shoulders a very small amount.

10
00:01:03.301 --> 00:01:05.301
Notice the effort of lifting.

11
00:01:07.001 --> 00:01:09.961
Then stop lifting and let gravity choose where they land.

12
00:01:11.661 --> 00:01:16.911
This is not a command to relax; it is a chance to feel the contrast between doing and not doing.

13
00:01:33.455 --> 00:01:36.855
Try the movement once more, perhaps one shoulder at a time.

14
00:01:38.555 --> 00:01:39.905
Lift slightly.

15
00:01:41.605 --> 00:01:42.175
Pause.

16
00:01:43.875 --> 00:01:45.665
Release the action.

17
00:01:47.365 --> 00:01:50.415
Notice whether any effort continues after the movement ends.

18
00:02:06.958 --> 00:02:08.058
Bring attention to the jaw.

19
00:02:09.758 --> 00:02:12.778
Feel where the upper and lower teeth meet, or the space between them.

20
00:02:14.478 --> 00:02:18.518
Notice the tongue, lips, cheeks, and hinges near the ears.

21
00:02:20.218 --> 00:02:22.668
You do not need to open the mouth or change the bite.

22
00:02:37.558 --> 00:02:42.288
If it is comfortable, let the lips part a little and move the jaw gently from side to side.

23
00:02:43.988 --> 00:02:45.238
Keep the range easy.

24
00:02:46.938 --> 00:02:50.468
Then let the jaw settle in a position that asks for no extra holding.

25
00:03:07.011 --> 00:03:10.571
Notice whether the tongue is pressing, hovering, or resting.

26
00:03:12.271 --> 00:03:14.961
Let it choose a broad, ordinary place in the mouth.

27
00:03:16.661 --> 00:03:18.201
Swallow if you need to.

28
00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:23.071
Feel the jaw again without checking whether it is relaxed enough.

29
00:03:39.615 --> 00:03:40.975
Now feel both hands.

30
00:03:42.675 --> 00:03:46.805
Notice the backs, palms, fingers, and spaces between fingers.

31
00:03:48.505 --> 00:03:52.255
Are the hands holding one another, clothing, a device, or nothing?

32
00:03:53.955 --> 00:03:58.495
If you are holding something safely, sense the exact amount of pressure being used.

33
00:04:13.384 --> 00:04:17.244
Slowly curl the fingers toward the palms without making a tight fist.

34
00:04:18.944 --> 00:04:20.794
Feel the work of closing.

35
00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:25.064
Then uncurl them and let the fingers find their own shape.

36
00:04:41.608 --> 00:04:45.658
Touch each fingertip to the thumb, one at a time, or imagine the sequence.

37
00:04:47.358 --> 00:04:52.298
Notice texture, temperature, and the precise beginning and ending of each contact.

38
00:05:08.842 --> 00:05:10.972
Let the hands rest again.

39
00:05:12.672 --> 00:05:17.482
Trace a line of sensation from fingers through wrists and forearms to the shoulders.

40
00:05:19.182 --> 00:05:23.232
The hands, jaw, and shoulders may influence one another, or they may not.

41
00:05:24.932 --> 00:05:26.612
There is no result to manufacture.

42
00:05:47.291 --> 00:05:48.841
Take one ordinary breath.

43
00:05:50.541 --> 00:05:54.021
As you exhale, stop any movement you are still making.

44
00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:58.771
Notice what the body does when the instructions become quiet.

45
00:06:19.451 --> 00:06:26.961
Include the whole body around these three areas: feet or seat supported, breath moving, room nearby.

46
00:06:28.661 --> 00:06:31.601
Shoulders, jaw, and hands do not need to remain soft.

47
00:06:33.301 --> 00:06:37.571
You have simply met them with attention and a little more choice.

48
00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:53.760
Let the eyes take in the room.

49
00:06:55.460 --> 00:07:00.000
Make the next movement slowly enough to notice it, and continue with whatever comes next.
